1. Test Levels

There are four main test levels:
1.Unit Testing – Testing individual components of the software. It is usually done by developers.
2.Integration Testing – Testing whether different modules work together correctly.
3.System Testing – Testing the complete integrated software.
4.Acceptance Testing – Testing whether the software meets user and business requirements. It is usually done by end-users or clients. 

2. Test Process

The test process mainly consists of:
1.Planning – Decide the testing objectives, scope, resources, schedule, risks, and testing strategy.
2.Monitoring – Track testing progress, test metrics, defects, and risks.
3.Control – Take corrective actions, manage changes, track defects, and adjust resources when needed.  

